/ Observatory ships its own layout.
/
/ It would be tempting to render inside the host's admin layout and inherit its
/ navigation for free. That couples the engine to every route helper the host's
/ layout happens to call — `searches_path`, and whatever is added next — and an
/ isolated engine resolves helpers against its own routes, so those raise. More
/ importantly it would make the engine unextractable: a gem cannot depend on a
/ layout it does not ship.
/
/ So the chrome is self-contained. It pulls the host's compiled stylesheet, which
/ is the one thing worth borrowing, and degrades to readable unstyled HTML
/ without it.
doctype html
html lang='en'
  head
    title
      = [ content_for(:title), 'Observatory' ].compact.join(' · ')
    meta charset='UTF-8'
    meta content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1' name='viewport'
    meta name='robots' content='noindex, nofollow'
    = csrf_meta_tags
    = csp_meta_tag

    - if respond_to?(:vite_stylesheet_tag)
      = vite_stylesheet_tag('application.css')
      = vite_client_tag
      = vite_javascript_tag('application')

  body.text-white.text-sm.font-light.font-sans.antialiased class="bg-[#0b0d12]"
    header class="border-b border-white/5"
      .container.mx-auto.px-6.py-4
        .row.items-center.justify-between.flex-wrap.gap-4
          .row.items-baseline.gap-3
            = link_to('Observatory', root_path, class: 'text-base font-light text-white tracking-wide')
            span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-600"
              = Rails.env

          nav.row.items-center.gap-1
            - { root_path => 'Overview', incidents_path => 'Incidents', requests_path => 'Requests',
                routes_path => 'Routes', jobs_path => 'Sidekiq' }.each do |path, label|
              - active = request.path == path || (path != root_path && request.path.start_with?(path))
              = link_to(label, path, class: "px-3 py-1.5 text-xs rounded #{ active ? 'bg-white/10 text-white' : 'text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-200' }")

          - if (back = Observatory.back_link_path)
            = link_to(Observatory.config.back_link_label, back, class: 'text-xs text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-400')

    main.container.mx-auto.px-6.py-8
      = yield

    footer class="container mx-auto px-6 py-8 border-t border-white/5 mt-8"
      .row.flex-wrap.items-center.justify-between.gap-3
        span class="text-[11px] text-gray-600"
          | Observatory v#{ Observatory::VERSION } · #{ Observatory::Release.current }
        span class="text-[11px] text-gray-600"
          | Allocation and GC figures are process-wide estimates. CRuby has no per-thread counter.
